      "body": "Dividend of ₹0.80 is 33% higher than last year. Ex-date: 22nd May 2026 Payment date: 11th July 2026 Dividend yield will be 0.1%, which is lower than the industry average of 0.8%. Sustainability & Growth Dividend is covered by earnings (5% earnings payout ratio) but the company has no free cash flows available, indicating it may be using cash reserves or debt to pay the dividend. The dividend has increased by an average of 32% per year over the past 10 years and has been stable with no material reductions to payments, indicating a long track record of dividend growth and stability. EPS is expected to grow by 33% over the next 2 years, which should provide support to the dividend and adequate earnings cover.",
